\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Task and task law}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{agent}
\tag{probability}

\p{Let #{\mathcal T} be a measurable set of task descriptions. A
\strong{task} #{q\in\mathcal T} specifies the public problem statement and
the success criterion used for that instance. A \strong{task law}
#{\mathcal Q} is a probability distribution on #{\mathcal T}.}

\p{This is an FTIP synthesis of the task-indexed interaction described in
Chapter 3 of \citef{sutton2018reinforcement} and the POMDP setup in
\citet{Section 2}{kaelbling1998planning}. The task description
does not include hidden environment state or the evaluator's private answer.
Those objects receive separate types below.}

\p{A task law says how instances are sampled. It does not imply that training
and evaluation use the same law. That distinction is deferred to
\ref{ftip-002F}.}
